1
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:17,944
And now, the World Number One Police Championship.
The second event is here,

2
00:00:17,994 --> 00:00:21,720
the shooting competition on the Nazca
Highlands of Peru in South America.

3
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:25,656
Twelve competitors who made it through
the first event's race will compete,

4
00:00:25,706 --> 00:00:27,874
first, Kaipan Deka,
winner of the first event,

5
00:00:27,924 --> 00:00:30,420
hit the target perfectly on the
first shot for a flawless 100 points.

6
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:34,860
Next, representing Japan as well, is Ryotsu.

7
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:39,460
Go for it!

8
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:51,000
Ryotsu scores 95 points.

9
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,640
Looks like he missed a bit.

10
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:54,480
So close for Ryotsu!

11
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:56,000
He finished with 95 points.

12
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:00,260
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

13
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:02,120
Whoa, a Manhattan-sized one!

14
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:04,480
He has pushed Ryotsu
aside and stepped forward.

15
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:07,840
What is that gun?

16
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:11,420
The FBI and NASA secretly co-developed it.

17
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,200
It's the latest model laser gun.

18
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:15,120
It has no trigger.

19
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:18,240
Just by looking at the
target through the goggles,

20
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:30,320
This is amazing.

21
00:01:32,420 --> 00:01:34,080
Come on, just start the thing.

22
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:35,560
Wait a minute!

23
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:36,600
What?

24
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:40,520
Isn't a computer-rigged gun
like this against the rules?

25
00:01:41,260 --> 00:01:44,160
The rules say any gun
you bring is fine, right?

26
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:45,320
It's not against the rules.

27
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:48,780
Don't you have any
pride as a police officer?

28
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:51,520
At this rate, it's not you using the gun,

29
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:56,860
but the gun using you, isn't it?
Ryotsu has a point there.

30
00:01:56,860 --> 00:02:03,960
This competition tests the shooter's skill, not the gun's performance.
It's not a rule violation.

31
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:07,860
No problem there.
I'll continue the competition. Dokyuraa!

32
00:02:07,860 --> 00:02:10,940
Yeah, come on, start it already.

33
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:16,860
Damn it, if it's come to this, then...

34
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:23,700
Excuse me for a moment.

35
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:26,000
Hello, hello?

36
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:28,980
What's the matter?

37
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:32,820
There's a call for Manhattan Deka.

38
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:35,860
Manhattan Deka, Manhattan Deka.

39
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:39,840
There's a call coming in
for the commentary booth.

40
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:43,280
What is it at a time like this?

41
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:46,980
Sorry.

42
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:47,840
Go ahead.

43
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:52,240
Yes, this is Manhattan Deka
of the New York City Police.

44
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:53,280
What?

45
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:55,620
Three ramen and three gyoza.

46
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:58,120
I'm not a Chinese restaurant.

47
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,100
It's a wrong number.

48
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:01,360
I see.

49
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:06,840
You did something, didn't you?

50
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:08,860
I didn't do anything.

51
00:03:11,540 --> 00:03:13,100
Alright, get started.

52
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:24,800
The data is getting corrupted.

53
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:33,960
Manhattan Deka! What kind of
accident was that? He suddenly left.

54
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:35,540
He's retired, sir.

55
00:03:36,540 --> 00:03:39,080
I knew you did something.

56
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:41,260
I didn't do anything, I'm telling you.

57
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:46,160
Personally,
I'd like to knock that guy out early.

58
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:48,200
I'll turn a blind eye to it.

59
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:51,380
I already told you, I didn't do anything.

60
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:54,020
Actually, back then...

61
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:57,000
Manhattan Deka, Manhattan Deka!

62
00:03:59,620 --> 00:04:00,920
What is it at a time like this?

63
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:11,800
Just in case something like this happened,
I had Denkyoku Plus make it.

64
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:14,500
this computer virus generator.

65
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:19,100
That ramen, and gyoza, please.

66
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,980
That's the story.

67
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:34,980
Nakagawa's ringer, Volvo Saigo.

68
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:37,460
With his superb shooting skill,
he gets a perfect 100 points!

69
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:46,500
Savanna Deka, who loves nature, has
dared to score 100 points with a blowgun!

70
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:51,300
Crocodile Deka.

71
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:52,720
98 points.

72
00:04:56,340 --> 00:04:57,340
Cossack Deka.

73
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:58,620
96 points.

74
00:04:58,620 --> 00:05:00,260
Ramen Deka.

75
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:01,800
97 points

76
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:03,140
Scotch Deka

77
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:04,360
99 points

78
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:06,940
That concludes the second event.

79
00:05:06,940 --> 00:05:09,460
The top eight advance to the third event.

80
00:05:09,460 --> 00:05:10,420
Taipan Deka

81
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:11,600
Nakagawa

82
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:12,620
Savanna Deka

83
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:13,540
Scotch Deka

84
00:05:13,540 --> 00:05:14,840
Crocodile Deka

85
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:15,840
Ramen Deka

86
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:17,060
Cossack Deka

87
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:18,500
And Ryotsu, of course.

88
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:24,560
Manhattan Deka, a favorite to win,
has suddenly retired,

89
00:05:25,020 --> 00:05:26,480
I wonder what the cause was.

90
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:35,780
Chobary

91
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:40,200
Nakagawa is using his reinforcement,
Sakonji,

92
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:43,680
and has also made it through the third event,
the mixed martial arts match!

93
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:49,180
Crocodile Deka pins Savanna Deka
with a magnificent backdrop drop!

94
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:53,080
Wow...

95
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:58,720
Player 4 launches a fierce
attack with his specialty, kendo!

96
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:01,120
Ramen Deka is purely on the defensive!

97
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:02,600
Three minutes have passed.

98
00:06:03,140 --> 00:06:04,220
This is getting unbearable.

99
00:06:09,620 --> 00:06:11,360
Nya~, it's done, aru~!

100
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:14,160
It hurts.

101
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:14,640
Wi...

102
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:15,700
Shuuu...

103
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:16,440
Shuuu...

104
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:21,140
Here it comes, here it comes, here it comes!

105
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:24,200
W-what?

106
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:27,460
If I eat ramen,
I'll be 100 times more energetic, aru.

107
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:32,330
Come on,

108
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:43,260
are you going to give up?

109
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:50,720
No good, I'm losing consciousness.

110
00:06:50,720 --> 00:06:52,080
Senpai...

111
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:55,640
Senpai, please pull yourself together!

112
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:58,000
You're giving up on the 100 million yen?

113
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:02,740
That's right, it's the 100 million yen!

114
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:09,000
Take this!

115
00:07:11,660 --> 00:07:12,860
Yes!

116
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:15,200
Alright!

117
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:15,820
Shaaah!

118
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:18,680
Ryotsu advances to the semifinals!

119
00:07:19,140 --> 00:07:22,380
He really turns superhuman when
there's big money on the line!

120
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:23,241
Now then,

121
00:07:23,291 --> 00:07:28,700
the final match is between Japan's
Kaipan Deka and Britain's Scotch Deka!

122
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:32,220
Which one will make it
through to the semifinals?

123
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:36,780
Here it comes! Golden Claw!

124
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:42,320
Decided in an instant!
Kaipan Deka is the winner!

125
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:45,540
Not that again.

126
00:07:45,540 --> 00:07:47,460
Crazy!

127
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,780
And now,
the World Number One Police Championship!

128
00:07:51,780 --> 00:07:57,160
The semifinal takes place here in Antarctica:
a five-hour endurance penguin tailing race.

129
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:00,440
The rules are simple.

130
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:04,640
If you succeed in tailing the fleeing
penguin robot by dog sled for five hours,

131
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:06,240
you advance to the final.

132
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:09,300
What, that's easy!

133
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:10,380
Handshake

134
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:15,100
When anyone comes within 30 meters,

135
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:17,320
the penguins automatically turn around.

136
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:21,300
If a penguin notices you,
the tailing is a failure.

137
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:25,080
I'm bringing Kangaroo Deka
along as my reinforcement.

138
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:26,700
Gorgor!

139
00:08:26,700 --> 00:08:29,320
I'll have Honda accompany me too.

140
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:30,420
Brr, so so so cold!

141
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:33,880
Nakagawa, in the second and third events,

142
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:36,220
you both already used your reinforcements,
didn't you?

143
00:08:36,780 --> 00:08:38,760
I understand. I'll do it alone.

144
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:41,400
Kaipan Deka, what about your reinforcement?

145
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:44,720
I might call one later,
but for now I'll go alone.

146
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:49,340
And now, the five-hour endurance
penguin tailing race begins!

147
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:58,340
We will track each player's penguin robot.

148
00:09:05,820 --> 00:09:07,780
It's colder than I expected.

149
00:09:08,140 --> 00:09:09,380
I feel like my body's going to freeze.

150
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:29,460
Nakagawa has been disqualified.

151
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:30,860
Damn it.

152
00:09:30,860 --> 00:09:34,120
Nakagawa has retired early!

153
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:39,080
Nakagawa was the only conscience
of the Japanese police...

154
00:09:43,380 --> 00:09:44,540
We won't let you get away!

155
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:45,640
Garu garu!

156
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:57,800
We'll show you the power of
Australia's strongest duo!

157
00:09:58,100 --> 00:09:58,620
Garu garu!

158
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:02,420
Go! Kangaroo Deka!

159
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:03,280
Garu garu!

160
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:07,740
Kangaroo!

161
00:10:12,560 --> 00:10:14,060
I'll deliver the final blow!

162
00:10:21,980 --> 00:10:23,680
Come on, let's chase the penguins!

163
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:24,420
Garu garu!

164
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:44,120
Damn it! That red penguin! What speed!

165
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:46,660
If they pull away any more,
we'll lose sight of them!

166
00:10:46,780 --> 00:10:48,680
Honda! Take the reins!

167
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:51,760
N-no way... Ah ah ah...

168
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:54,380
I came prepared for just this kind of thing!

169
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:55,780
Damn it!

170
00:10:56,640 --> 00:10:57,580
Here! Honda!

171
00:11:00,580 --> 00:11:04,100
Whoa! Oi! A dog!
Tartar, stop running around!

172
00:11:05,380 --> 00:11:07,700
If we lose the penguin,
you won't get off easy!

173
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:14,360
With this,
advancing to the finals is a sure thing!

174
00:11:21,940 --> 00:11:24,740
Damn! I didn't expect
it to flee into the sea!

175
00:11:24,740 --> 00:11:26,860
What now? Go in after it in our swim trunks?

176
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:29,220
We'll bring in reinforcements here.

177
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:34,460
Requesting transport.

178
00:11:40,260 --> 00:11:41,860
It's too cold, so no factory stops.

179
00:11:41,860 --> 00:11:43,380
Hurry and get on, Kaipan Deka!

180
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:51,660
Thank goodness you're here, Dolphin Deka!

181
00:11:51,660 --> 00:11:54,440
Now that I'm here, you're in good hands.

182
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:01,540
Now, the five-hour endurance
penguin tailing race...

183
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:02,760
is finally over.

184
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:04,220
Five seconds to go!

185
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:07,940
3, 2, 1, goal!

186
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:10,240
Yeah! We did it!

187
00:12:11,460 --> 00:12:14,860
Japan's Ryotsu has advanced to the
final with a brilliant performance!

188
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:17,740
Got left behind again.

189
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:20,400
Also, according to information just in,

190
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:22,175
Japan's seeded Kaipan Deka,

191
00:12:22,225 --> 00:12:24,660
with the help of reinforcement Dolphin Deka,

192
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:26,200
has safely reached the goal!

193
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:27,960
Fight!

194
00:12:29,380 --> 00:12:31,120
That means the final will be

195
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:33,360
Ryotsu versus Kaipan Deka!

196
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:48,980
These two are notorious Japanese-American
gangsters on international wanted lists,

197
00:12:48,980 --> 00:12:52,320
and we have information that they've
been hiding in Tokyo for three days.

198
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:56,320
World Number One Police Championship Final.

199
00:12:57,960 --> 00:13:03,320
Simply put, the challenge is to arrest these two
vicious gangsters within the next twelve hours.

200
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:05,940
I see, sounds interesting.

201
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:10,280
Doesn't matter,
but why do they make us dress like this?

202
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:16,540
Well, for this kind of final, it's always
a tuxedo on a skyscraper rooftop, right?

203
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:18,580
It's just like Ultra Quiz, isn't it?

204
00:13:18,580 --> 00:13:24,420
By the way, if we arrest those two, we
really get the 100 million yen prize, right?

205
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:27,520
Of course. Please look behind you.

206
00:13:30,660 --> 00:13:33,920
Wow, that's amazing,
100 million yen in cash?

207
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:35,500
Got it.

208
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:38,340
You're awfully fixated on the prize money,
aren't you?

209
00:13:38,340 --> 00:13:41,500
What exactly are you planning
to spend 100 million yen on?

210
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:45,840
I'm going to buy a lifetime supply of
the same shoes Kaipan is wearing right now!

211
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:47,340
Do whatever you want.

212
00:13:47,760 --> 00:13:50,180
Then, are you both ready?

213
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:55,440
Wait a minute, is that mugshot the
only clue we have on the criminals?

214
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:57,240
Yes, that's right.

215
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:00,180
What? Even so, with just that alone...

216
00:14:00,180 --> 00:14:04,680
Hahaha, Kaipan Deka! If it's too much for you,
you can always drop out, you know.

217
00:14:04,680 --> 00:14:05,400
What did you say?

218
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:10,560
Hmph. Looks like the time has
come to play my last trump card.

219
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:11,220
Alright.

220
00:14:11,780 --> 00:14:13,200
Last trump card?

221
00:14:13,420 --> 00:14:15,720
What's Ryotsu planning to pull out?

222
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:18,060
Okay, it's your turn now.

223
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:20,120
Yeah.

224
00:14:20,540 --> 00:14:21,500
Mr. Higurashi.

225
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:24,700
Hey, Higurashi! Wake up. Wake up!

226
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:27,820
J-just let me sleep a little longer...

227
00:14:27,820 --> 00:14:29,000
Wake up.

228
00:14:31,240 --> 00:14:37,460
Ryotsu,
I feel like I haven't had enough sleep.

229
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:39,840
What year is it now?

230
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:44,340
It's the Athens Olympics year,
so it's obviously 2004.

231
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:46,940
The women's marathon is on right now.

232
00:14:46,940 --> 00:14:51,420
Japan's Shinobu Tazawa has entered
the main stadium in first place.

233
00:14:51,420 --> 00:14:54,400
Listen to this cheering!

234
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:58,520
Is she just about to win
back-to-back gold medals?

235
00:14:58,520 --> 00:15:00,780
This voice sounds familiar somehow.

236
00:15:01,680 --> 00:15:03,540
That's some kind of mistake.

237
00:15:03,540 --> 00:15:06,460
You just woke up and
you're still spacing out.

238
00:15:06,460 --> 00:15:08,840
Never mind that, let's get straight to work.

239
00:15:09,780 --> 00:15:12,820
Ryotsu-san, is this person the other helper?

240
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:14,180
That's right.

241
00:15:16,220 --> 00:15:20,360
Use your psychic powers to see
where these guys are right now!

242
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:22,720
I could really go for a hot coffee.

243
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:32,540
You only work once a year and you still complain about luxuries!
But when my head's all fuzzy, nothing comes to mind, that's all.

244
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:39,840
Honestly! Look, Higurashi, a gorgeous bunny
girl is counting on your psychic powers!

245
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:44,180
Aaaahhh!

246
00:15:45,980 --> 00:15:48,580
Alright, now I'm getting fired up!

247
00:15:48,580 --> 00:15:50,580
Okay, now look, look!

248
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:57,720
They're here! They're here!

249
00:15:58,340 --> 00:16:00,300
Both of them are nearby!

250
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,280
Nearby, you say?

251
00:16:03,780 --> 00:16:04,220
That's...

252
00:16:05,380 --> 00:16:06,740
That way!

253
00:16:10,460 --> 00:16:12,060
What, the building next door?

254
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:21,280
Kase!

255
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:26,900
What the... those guys! They're doing
something on the rooftop over there too!

256
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:30,163
What did you say!?

257
00:16:30,213 --> 00:16:35,240
On the rooftop over there, the World
Number One Gang Championship is being held!

258
00:16:35,660 --> 00:16:36,980
What did you just say!?

259
00:16:37,820 --> 00:16:40,920
Ugh, there are a bunch of
dangerous-looking guys gathered!

260
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:46,700
And the prize money is double ours,
200 million yen!

261
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:53,740
So they've been doing that kind of thing...
which means the culprits are among them

262
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:57,620
Right, in that case, first come, first served!
With Kaipan Deka, ga -

263
00:16:57,620 --> 00:17:04,220
Wait, the culprits are even closer than that!
Hey, help me!

264
00:17:06,120 --> 00:17:16,740
Whoa, Chief, what are you doing up there? And you're naked too!
I thought someone knocked you out on your way here, and this is the state you're in!

265
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:19,600
Then who's the Chief over here?

266
00:17:20,860 --> 00:17:21,980
Don't move!

267
00:17:24,220 --> 00:17:25,100
Chief!

268
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:26,320
When did you get here?

269
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:27,900
You! Who are you?

270
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:34,860
Whoa! You're the wanted criminal!

271
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:37,060
You switched places with the Chief!

272
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:40,040
You noticed a bit too late.

273
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:41,700
Hey! Bunny girl!

274
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:44,740
Bring the 100 million yen
duralumin case over here!

275
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:45,320
Y-yes!

276
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:49,500
Hurry up.

277
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:55,660
Wait!

278
00:17:55,660 --> 00:18:05,280
You're the other wanted fugitive,
aren't you?

279
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:10,740
Our final round was about
stealing your prize money!

280
00:18:10,740 --> 00:18:13,120
We're taking this 100 million yen!

281
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:21,260
Damn it! If they take the championship prize,
there's no point in fighting!

282
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:24,600
Kaipan Deka,
let's just split the prize money.

283
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:27,500
Let's team up and take the money back!

284
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:28,880
Fine by me.

285
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:33,540
Hey, I'm calling in my second backup now!

286
00:18:33,540 --> 00:18:35,000
Here you go.

287
00:18:35,820 --> 00:18:38,240
Moonlight Deka, we need backup!

288
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:39,500
That was fast!

289
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:42,160
So fast!

290
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:53,500
Thanks for your work, Moonlight Deka.

291
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:55,560
Where's Venus Deka?

292
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:58,480
Only two reinforcements are allowed,
you know.

293
00:18:58,480 --> 00:19:00,460
Venus Deka is off today.

294
00:19:01,620 --> 00:19:02,980
W-what is this?

295
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:05,160
You wear that instead.

296
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:06,420
Why me?

297
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,560
I can't do anything without an assistant.

298
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:10,900
You wear it.

299
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:14,900
If I become a reinforcement's reinforcement,
what's the point of reinforcements?

300
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:18,000
If you're not into it, I'm going home.

301
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Fine, I'll cut it, okay? I'll cut it!

302
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:27,400
Ahahaha!
It's not just a dazzling transformation!

303
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:31,700
Bathing my back in the moon's energy,
I'll tear evil apart with my justice stick!

304
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:34,380
If it's an incident in the sky,
leave it to me.

305
00:19:34,860 --> 00:19:39,920
Messenger from the moon,
Moonlight Deka, now appearing!

306
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:43,560
Gas or whatever, bring it on! If it's come to this,
might as well go all out!

307
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:46,580
W-what the heck? Who are those guys...

308
00:19:46,580 --> 00:19:47,760
Zzt... zzt...

309
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:51,540
Leave the machine guns to me!
Take this, you gangsters!

310
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:57,880
A machine gun like that won't work on me!

311
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:23,220
What are you doing, Kaipan Deka?

312
00:20:23,220 --> 00:20:25,820
We can't beat a helicopter
in turning ability.

313
00:20:29,680 --> 00:20:31,220
They've got us from behind!

314
00:20:33,280 --> 00:20:35,700
Hey, hey, hey, that help from before!

315
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:39,940
Alright, Ryo-two, we're transforming!

316
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:41,660
Now of all times?

317
00:20:43,060 --> 00:20:44,440
Make up!

318
00:20:44,820 --> 00:20:46,540
Moonlight Power!

319
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:49,320
Allow me to explain myself here!

320
00:20:49,500 --> 00:20:52,620
By transforming into Ocho without limit,
Moonlight Deka

321
00:20:52,620 --> 00:20:56,320
can fire an incredible bullet serve!

322
00:21:00,700 --> 00:21:01,760
A ball?!

323
00:21:02,220 --> 00:21:03,640
Let's go, Hiromi!

324
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:05,060
It's Hiromi?!

325
00:21:10,900 --> 00:21:12,080
Aaaaaah!

326
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:15,100
Eeeeeeh!

327
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:28,660
It's falling toward the Shinjuku Gyoen side!

328
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:41,640
Whoa, the bullets are
heading toward the pond too!

329
00:21:49,620 --> 00:21:50,320
Senpai!

330
00:21:50,640 --> 00:21:51,760
Ry-Ryotsu!

331
00:21:59,500 --> 00:22:01,440
Senpai! You're alive!

332
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:02,660
Thank goodness!

333
00:22:11,060 --> 00:22:14,364
Look! We arrested two of
the wanted criminals and

334
00:22:14,414 --> 00:22:16,260
took back the 100 million yen!

335
00:22:16,580 --> 00:22:17,440
Senpai...

336
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:21,540
The champion is Japan's representative,
Kankichi Ryotsu!

337
00:22:21,540 --> 00:22:22,740
We did it!

338
00:22:24,400 --> 00:22:25,600
Congratulations.

339
00:22:25,600 --> 00:22:28,120
Congratulations, Senpai. Ryotsu.

340
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:34,820
Being alive after all that,
he's really something.

341
00:22:34,820 --> 00:22:38,040
What an incredible tenacity. I lose.

342
00:22:38,040 --> 00:22:40,540
Well, time to head back to
the Special Crimes Division.

343
00:22:40,540 --> 00:22:43,020
Alright, let's hold a consolation party.

344
00:22:43,020 --> 00:22:44,140
That sounds good.

345
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:56,980
We hereby commend you for this.

346
00:22:56,980 --> 00:22:59,460
April 6, 2003

347
00:22:59,460 --> 00:23:01,500
Secretary-General of Interpol

348
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:03,000
It's 2003?

349
00:23:05,380 --> 00:23:06,500
Higurashi!

350
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:09,300
It's not even an Olympic year.

351
00:23:09,300 --> 00:23:10,840
How dare you wake me up like this!

352
00:23:10,840 --> 00:23:13,520
Wa-wa-wait! Calm down, Higurashi!

353
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:14,640
No excuses!

354
00:23:23,040 --> 00:23:24,960
Not nearly enough.

355
00:24:02,700 --> 00:24:04,860
This has turned into quite a mess,
hasn't it.

356
00:24:05,340 --> 00:24:09,280
Ryotsu, the 100 million yen prize
won't come close to covering the damages.

357
00:24:09,280 --> 00:24:11,600
M-me? I have to pay for it?

358
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:13,420
Obviously.

359
00:24:16,760 --> 00:24:18,320
I'm getting sleepy.

360
00:24:18,320 --> 00:24:19,440
Good night.

361
00:24:26,080 --> 00:24:27,540
Whatever.

362
00:24:27,540 --> 00:24:30,460
There's no way I can pay for all that!

363
00:24:46,420 --> 00:24:53,120
Why does Lemon-chan,
a kindergartener, like period dramas?

364
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:59,260
I wonder why the Chief's little
mustache is slightly small.

365
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:07,180
I wonder why Honda-san's personality
changes when he rides a bike.

366
00:25:07,180 --> 00:25:08,800
I wonder why.

367
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:12,860
Why does Higurashi, the sleeping man,
only wake up once every four years?

368
00:25:12,860 --> 00:25:14,020
I wonder why.

369
00:25:14,020 --> 00:25:16,120
I wonder why.

370
00:25:16,860 --> 00:25:23,140
Nakagawa won't lend money to Ryo-san,

371
00:25:23,140 --> 00:25:26,900
but he lends out tanks
and fighter jets so easily.

372
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:30,180
I wonder why.

373
00:25:32,720 --> 00:25:37,520
Reiko is incredibly rich,

374
00:25:39,140 --> 00:25:43,080
so why does she work at the police box?
I wonder why.

375
00:25:43,840 --> 00:25:46,560
I wonder why, I wonder why.

376
00:25:47,160 --> 00:25:50,160
I wonder why, I wonder why,
I wonder why, I wonder why.

